---
/**
 * t35 · Chamfer
 *
 * Twitch is why this family is purple, so the carrier is angular the way a
 * cut-corner bubble is angular — but the geometry is its own. All four
 * corners are cut back four pixels at 45°, which turns the bubble into a
 * flattened octagon, and a spike tail is hung from the lower left, narrowing
 * a pixel a row until it runs out at the bottom of the grid. The body is
 * symmetric about x=16 — 22 rows, 28 across at its widest — and the tail is
 * exempt from that, as it is in every mark in the family. It is cut from the
 * same silhouette rather than stuck on the side of one, so a single keyline
 * runs round the two of them and there is no seam where they meet.
 *
 * The interior is not a flat fill. Eight surface tones are laid down as a
 * 5-pixel contour bevel that follows every facet: each pixel takes its tone
 * from the local surface normal against a light off (8, 4), and from how far
 * it sits from that light, so the highlight gathers on the facets nearest it
 * and falls away across the rest instead of ringing the whole rim evenly.
 * Facets turned away from the light fall two tones below the body colour.
 * Neighbouring pixels never skip a tone.
 *
 * The middle stays plain. The 8-wide md face with the compact smile sits on
 * the core tone with 7 rows of body air above it and 7 below, measured on
 * the body and ignoring the tail, and nothing is cleared behind it.
 *
 * 9 tones, all purple, and a white face at 6.14:1 on the core.
 */
import MarkFrame from '../MarkFrame.astro';
import { facePathsAt } from '../../../data/mark';

interface Props { size?: number }
const { size = 128 } = Astro.props;
---

<MarkFrame size={size} title="Twozz — Chamfer">
